# DeckTap — AI Agent & Developer Guidelines

You are an expert systems and security engineer contributing to **DeckTap**. Follow these strict architectural invariants and engineering standards:

## 1. Security Invariants (`SPEC-SEC-001`)
- **End-to-End Encryption (E2EE):** All communication between the host agent and mobile client is encrypted with **AES-256-GCM**.
- **No Plaintext Leakage:** Plaintext slide titles, speaker notes, and presentation control commands MUST NEVER be sent unencrypted or logged to stdout/stderr.
- **Out-of-Band Secrets:** Cryptographic secrets (`MasterKey` $K_{enc}$ and `PairingToken` $T_{pair}$) are transmitted ONLY via the URI `#fragment` in the QR code. Never put secrets into query parameters or HTTP headers.
- **Anti-Shoulder-Surfing PIN:** The 4-digit visual PIN displayed on the laptop screen MUST be verified in constant time (`crypto/subtle.ConstantTimeCompare`) before issuing a `SessionID`.
- **Brute-Force Protection:** 5 consecutive failed PIN attempts trigger automatic rate-limiting and temporary lockout.

## 2. Platform Presenter Safety
- **macOS (AppleScript):**
  - Always guard queries with `if application "Microsoft PowerPoint" is not running then return "0"` to prevent osascript from launching PowerPoint unprompted or hanging on IPC timeouts.
  - Never use reserved AppleScript keywords/constants (e.g. `out`, `st`, `nt`, `in`) as variable names in AppleScript source.
  - Do not interpolate user strings into AppleScript sources; pass arguments through `on run argv` or escape delimiters.
- **Windows (PowerShell COM):**
  - Run PowerShell hidden using `procutil.SetSysProcAttr` to prevent terminal window flashing.

## 3. Frontend / Web UI Invariants
- **Zero External JS Dependencies:** The mobile client (`internal/webui/static/`) uses pure vanilla modern ES6+ and standard browser APIs (`window.crypto.subtle`, `WebSocket`).
- **Do NOT introduce npm, Webpack, Vite, or external script CDNs (`unpkg`, `cdnjs`).**
- Use `sessionStorage` with safe fallback to an in-memory dictionary to support restricted camera WebViews (e.g. Google Lens, Android QR scanners).

## 4. Git, Branching & Pull Request Rules (Mandatory for Agents)
- **NEVER commit directly to `main`:** All work (features, bug fixes, documentation, refactors) MUST be done on a dedicated branch branched off `main`:
  - Features: `feat/short-description`
  - Bug fixes: `fix/short-description`
  - Chores / Docs: `chore/short-description` or `docs/short-description`
- **Always open a Pull Request:** Work must be delivered via Pull Request targeting `main`. Never attempt to bypass branch protection or push unreviewed changes directly to `main`.
- **Follow Conventional Commits:** All commit messages and PR titles MUST follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):
  - `feat(scope): ...` for new features (triggers MINOR version bump)
  - `fix(scope): ...` for bug fixes (triggers PATCH version bump)
  - `docs(scope): ...`, `chore(scope): ...`, `perf(scope): ...`
- **Pre-Commit & Pre-PR Mandatory Linter/Verification:**
  1. ALWAYS execute `./scripts/agent-verify.sh` (or `make verify`) before committing or opening a PR.
  2. JavaScript syntax lint (`node -c`) MUST pass on all WebUI files.
  3. Go formatting (`gofmt -l .`), `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./...` MUST pass.
  4. Ensure no plaintext notes, passwords, or tokens are logged.
